{"name":"Irritated Ibis","hex":"#ee1122","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"irritated","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of irritate"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Experiencing a feeling of irritation.","Inflamed and painful."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/irritated"},{"term":"ibis","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae, having long downcurved bills used to probe the mud for prey such as crustaceans."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ibis"}],"entries":[{"title":"Irritation","blocks":[{"text":"Irritation, in biology and physiology, is a state of inflammation or painful reaction to allergy or cell-lining damage. A stimulus or agent which induces the state of irritation is an irritant. Irritants are typically thought of as chemical agents but mechanical, thermal (heat), and radiative stimuli can also be irritants. Irritation also has non-clinical usages referring to bothersome physical or psychological pain or discomfort."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/ExclamationMark.png/330px-ExclamationMark.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Irritation"},{"title":"Ibis","blocks":[{"text":"The ibis are a group of long-legged wading birds in the family Threskiornithidae that inhabit wetlands, forests and plains. \"Ibis\" derives from the Latin and Ancient Greek word for this group of birds. It also occurs in the scientific name of the western cattle egret mistakenly identified in 1757 as being the sacred ibis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg/330px-Black-headed_Ibis_%28Threskiornis_melanocephalus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikiped